{#
  One person's archive, at `/author/{username}/`.

  decision-14 makes this URL their ActivityPub actor as well, so a peer asking
  for the actor and a reader asking for the page are at the same address; this
  is the page half of it. `author` is the profile — `name`, and whatever of
  `bio`, `avatar` and `links` they have written — and it is the same shape an
  entry's bio is given.

  The source design has no author archive, so there is nothing to port: the
  heading is the CMS's own. What it does not keep is an h-card of its own.
  `partials/bio.njk` is the one the theme has, and it prints the whole profile
  — the note and the `rel="me"` links — wherever it is, so this page is headed
  with the same card that ends each of their posts.
#}
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% set bioAuthor = author %}
{% set bioLead = "Posts by" %}

{% block title %}{{ author.name }}{% if pagination.pageNumber > 0 %}, page {{ pagination.pageNumber + 1 }}{% endif %} &middot; {{ site.title }}{% endblock %}

{% import "partials/feeds.njk" as feeds %}
{% block alternates %}
{{ super() }}
{{ feeds.feedLinks(author.url, site.title + ": " + author.name) }}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<header class="author-header">
  <h1 class="page-title">{{ author.name }}</h1>
</header>
{% include "partials/bio.njk" %}
{% include "partials/post-list.njk" %}
{% include "partials/pagination.njk" %}
{% endblock %}
